For example, you could have a .apk file with the following content:

```
// Package com.example.app
import android.app.Activity;

public class MainActivity extends Activity {
    @Override
    protected void onCreate(Bundle savedInstanceState) {
        super.onCreate(savedInstanceState);
        setContentView(R.layout.activity_main);
    }
}
```

And a .jar file with the following content (assuming it's a Java-based app):

```
// Package com.example.app
import java.io.*;

public class App {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("App started.");
    }
}
```

This code could be placed in a directory named 'src/com/example/app' or in a directory named 'app' in the app's package. When the app is installed, the jar file would be placed in the build directory, and the apk file would be placed in the app's source directory.

const loginForm = document.getElementById('login-form');
const usernameInput = document.getElementById('username');
const passwordInput = document.getElementById('password');
const loginButton = document.getElementById('submit-login');

loginForm.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const username = usernameInput.value.trim();
  const password = passwordInput.value.trim();

  // Check for empty fields
  if (!username || !password) {
    alert('Please fill in both your username and password.');
    return;
  }

  // Simulated API call (replace with actual backend logic)
  fetch('/api/login', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }),
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => {
      alert('Login successful! Welcome back, ' + username + '!');
      // Redirect user to dashboard or home page
      if (data.success) {
        if (data.dashboardId) {
          window.location.href = `dashboard/${data.dashboardId}`;
        } else {
          window.location.href = '/';
        }
      } else {
        alert('Invalid username or password.');
      }
    })
    .catch(error => {
      alert('Failed to log in. Please try again.');
    });
});

